# The classic worry in Meno's dispute is that "know" shifts. "That which he does not know" may mean lacking full knowledge of an answer, while "does not know the very subject" may mean being unable even to identify what is sought.
# That gap, if real, lies between two different claims (enq_unknown and knows_subject), linked by P7. Each claim is worded and meant the same way in every statement that uses it, so none is in two senses.
